{"description":"eka context --depth engineering (and eka get --upstream) fail with 'runtime: resolve: \"\u003ctype\u003e:\u003cid\u003e\" is an unqualified reference (missing the \u003cns\u003e/ prefix)' when the subject's neighborhood contains units whose relationship targets are unqualified (no namespace prefix). The store carries such targets (verified: e.g. eka/req:cli-experience derives-from 'req:prd', eka/req:prd derives-from 'str:self-hosting', eka/adr:012 depends-on 'adr:009-...'; 775 unqualified relationship targets in the workspace store as of 2026-08-15). The resolver rejects unqualified forms by design (eka-core runtime/resolver.go, TestResolverRejectsUnqualifiedForms), so the read path cannot traverse the graph for those subjects. Reproduction: eka context eka/req:eka-mcp-production --json fails with \"req:prd\" unqualified reference. Impact: the context-first constraint check (eka context --depth engineering), upstream traceability walks (eka get --upstream) and downstream queries are broken for most subjects of the eka project, because req:prd (the top requirement) and the ADR chain are referenced unqualified from many units. This is a live retrieval bug affecting every planning/discussion/execution session that relies on the context engine. Discovered during the fnd:rag-db-optimization planning session (2026-08-15); recorded in eka/fnd:rag-db-optimization investigationSummary. Not yet fixed in eka-core HEAD (verified 2026-08-15).","impact":"Blocking for the context-first workflow: eka context and eka get --upstream fail on the majority of subjects in the eka project (anything whose neighborhood touches req:prd, str:self-hosting, or the ADR chain). Planning sessions must fall back to manual domain queries (eka get discovery/architecture + per-line eka get), losing the constraint-closure guarantee of --depth engineering. Wrong results are not produced — commands refuse deterministically — but the retrieval surface is degraded. Fix candidates (to evaluate): (a) normalize unqualified relationship targets at publish/snapshot-compile time to the unit's namespace; (b) make the read-path resolver namespace-default unqualified forms against the referring unit; (c) re-seed/republish affected units with qualified targets. Option (c) conflicts with immutability (new revisions required); (a) is the preferred root fix."}